---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { methods } from "../../data/api";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const python = `import json, os, socket

request = {
    "method": "appearance",
    "value": json.dumps({"accent": "#c4b5fd", "gap": 16})
}
with socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX) as client:
    client.settimeout(3)
    client.connect(os.environ["LUDASH_CONTROL"])
    client.sendall(json.dumps(request).encode() + b"\\n")
    data = b""
    while b"\\n" not in data:
        chunk = client.recv(65536)
        if not chunk or len(data) + len(chunk) > 1024 * 1024:
            raise RuntimeError("Invalid LunaDash response")
        data += chunk
    response = json.loads(data)
    if "error" in response:
        raise RuntimeError(response["error"])
    print(response["appearance"])`;
---
<DocsLayout title="Talk to your desktop." section="api" summary="Use the local control socket, write a Quickshell component, or build an opt-in native effect. Each interface has a different scope and trust boundary.">
  <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#ipc">Local IPC</a><a href="#methods">Methods</a><a href="#qml">QML interface</a><a href="#native">Native plugins</a></nav>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>This is a local API, not an HTTP service.</strong> The website documents and previews configuration; it does not control your desktop. The compositor's Unix socket is restricted to the session user.</p></div>
  <h2 id="ipc">Start with ludashctl</h2><p>Applications launched inside LunaDash inherit <code>LUDASH_CONTROL</code>. For an external terminal, point it at your running session's socket. The default session name is <code>ludash-0</code>; substitute the name passed to <code>--socket</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={'export LUDASH_CONTROL="$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ludash-test-control"\n./build/ludashctl status\n./build/ludashctl appearance \'{"gap":16,"animations":true}\'\n./build/ludashctl open-settings modules'} />
  <p>Send one UTF-8 JSON object followed by a newline. <code>method</code> and <code>value</code> are strings; JSON-valued settings are encoded inside <code>value</code>. Numeric IDs are also sent as strings.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="WIRE REQUEST" code={'{"method":"appearance","value":"{\\"gap\\":16}"}\n'} />
  <p>A successful call generally returns an updated state object. Failure returns <code>{'{"error":"message"}'}</code>; the CLI exits nonzero. Audio and power helpers run asynchronously, so acceptance is not completion—poll status for busy/error fields. Requests are limited to 64 KiB with a three-second server deadline; a client should also bound response size and time.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="PYTHON / DIRECT SOCKET CLIENT" code={python} />
  <h2 id="methods">Control methods</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Value</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{methods.map(method => <tr><td class="api-method">{method.name}</td><td>{method.value}</td><td>{method.behavior}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <h2 id="qml">A small QML interface</h2><p>Each custom component receives <code>shell</code>, resolved <code>style</code>, and <code>moduleId</code>. Read <code>shell.state</code> as a snapshot and use commands for changes. The host manages the window, dimensions, animation and fallback content.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="QML / COMMON CALLS" code={'shell.launch("terminal")\nshell.launch("files")\nshell.command("workspace", 1)\nshell.setAppearance({ blur: true, blurRadius: 18 })\nshell.settingsOpen = true\nconst title = shell.focusedTitle\nconst label = shell.tr("Settings")'} />
  <p><a href={`${base}docs/modules/`}>The component guide</a> includes a complete Item template, JSON styles and recovery steps. Custom QML can execute processes and access files; metadata does not isolate it.</p>
  <h2 id="native">Native effect plugins · API 1</h2><p>Native plugins use the <code>LuDash::CompositorPlugin</code> interface. Implement <code>windowOpened(QQuickItem*)</code> and <code>windowFocused(QQuickItem*)</code> in a <code>QObject</code> subclass, declare <code>Q_INTERFACES</code>, and embed metadata with <code>Q_PLUGIN_METADATA</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="METADATA.JSON" code={JSON.stringify({KPlugin:{Id:"org.example.effect",Name:"Example effect",Version:"1.0.0",License:"GPL-3.0-only",EnabledByDefault:false},LuDash:{ApiVersion:1,Type:"WindowEffect",Library:"libexample-effect.so"}},null,2)} />
  <CodeBlock label="C++ / HEADER INTERFACE" code={'#include <QObject>\n#include <LuDash/plugins/CompositorPlugin.h>\n\nnamespace LuDash {\nclass ExampleEffect final : public QObject, public CompositorPlugin {\n    Q_OBJECT\n    Q_PLUGIN_METADATA(IID LUDASH_COMPOSITOR_PLUGIN_IID FILE "metadata.json")\n    Q_INTERFACES(LuDash::CompositorPlugin)\npublic:\n    void windowOpened(QQuickItem* frame) override;\n    void windowFocused(QQuickItem* frame) override;\n};\n}'} />
  <p>Put implementations in a matching <code>.cpp</code> file and build a CMake <code>MODULE</code> library linked to Qt Quick. Store the library and metadata together in <code>~/.local/share/ludash/plugins/&lt;id&gt;/</code>, enable it in Plugins, then restart the compositor. Keep retained window references in <code>QPointer</code> and never access a destroyed frame.</p>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Native code runs inside the compositor.</strong> Plugins are disabled by default. There is no sandbox or signing system, and a faulty plugin can crash the session. The metadata resembles KDE's structure; LunaDash does not implement KWin's ABI or load KWin plugins.</p></div>
  <p>The repository contains a complete <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/tree/main/src/compositor/plugins">fade effect implementation and header</a>, plus <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/blob/main/docs/PLUGINS.md">packaging instructions</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
